"1998-aime-1": { s: String.raw`For how many values of $k$ is $12^{12}$ the least common multiple of the positive integers $6^6,$ $8^8,$ and $k?$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-10": { s: String.raw`Eight spheres of radius $100$ are placed on a flat surface so that each sphere is tangent to two others and their centers are the vertices of a regular octagon. A ninth sphere is placed on the flat surface so that it is tangent to each of the other eight spheres. The radius of this last sphere is $a + b\sqrt{c},$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are positive integers, and $c$ is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find $a + b + c.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-11": { s: String.raw`Three of the edges of a cube are $\overline{AB},$ $\overline{BC},$ and $\overline{CD},$ and $\overline{AD}$ is an interior diagonal. Points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R$ are on $\overline{AB},$ $\overline{BC},$ and $\overline{CD},$ respectively, so that $AP = 5,$ $PB = 15,$ $BQ = 15,$ and $CR = 10.$ What is the area of the polygon that is the intersection of plane $PQR$ and the cube?`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-12": { s: String.raw`Let $ABC$ be equilateral, and $D,$ $E,$ and $F$ be the midpoints of $\overline{BC},$ $\overline{CA},$ and $\overline{AB},$ respectively. There exist points $P,$ $Q,$ and $R$ on $\overline{DE},$ $\overline{EF},$ and $\overline{FD},$ respectively, with the property that $P$ is on $\overline{CQ},$ $Q$ is on $\overline{AR},$ and $R$ is on $\overline{BP}.$ The ratio of the area of triangle $ABC$ to the area of triangle $PQR$ is $a + b\sqrt{c},$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are integers, and $c$ is not divisible by the square of any prime. What is $a^2 + b^2 + c^2?$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-13": { s: String.raw`If $\{a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots, a_n\}$ is a set of real numbers, indexed so that $a_1 \lt a_2 \lt a_3 \lt \cdots \lt a_n,$ its complex power sum is defined to be $a_1 i + a_2 i^2 + a_3 i^3 + \cdots + a_n i^n,$ where $i^2 = -1.$ Let $S_n$ be the sum of the complex power sums of all nonempty subsets of $\{1, 2, \ldots, n\}.$ Given that $S_8 = -176 - 64i$ and $S_9 = p + qi,$ where $p$ and $q$ are integers, find $|p| + |q|.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-14": { s: String.raw`An $m \times n \times p$ rectangular box has half the volume of an $(m + 2) \times (n + 2) \times (p + 2)$ rectangular box, where $m,$ $n,$ and $p$ are integers, and $m \le n \le p.$ What is the largest possible value of $p?$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-15": { s: String.raw`Define a domino to be an ordered pair of distinct positive integers. A proper sequence of dominos is a list of distinct dominos in which the first coordinate of each pair after the first equals the second coordinate of the immediately preceding pair, and in which $(i, j)$ and $(j, i)$ do not both appear for any $i$ and $j.$ Let $D_{40}$ be the set of all dominos whose coordinates are no larger than $40.$ Find the length of the longest proper sequence of dominos that can be formed using the dominos of $D_{40}.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-2": { s: String.raw`Find the number of ordered pairs $(x, y)$ of positive integers that satisfy $x \le 2y \le 60$ and $y \le 2x \le 60.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-3": { s: String.raw`The graph of $y^2 + 2xy + 40|x| = 400$ partitions the plane into several regions. What is the area of the bounded region?`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-4": { s: String.raw`Nine tiles are numbered $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ $\ldots,$ $9,$ respectively. Each of three players randomly selects and keeps three of the tiles, and sums those three values. The probability that all three players obtain an odd sum is $\frac{m}{n},$ where $m$ and $n$ are relatively prime positive integers. Find $m + n.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-5": { s: String.raw`Given that $A_k = \frac{k(k - 1)}{2}\cos\frac{k(k - 1)\pi}{2},$ find $|A_{19} + A_{20} + \cdots + A_{98}|.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-6": { s: String.raw`Let $ABCD$ be a parallelogram. Extend $\overline{DA}$ through $A$ to a point $P,$ and let $\overline{PC}$ meet $\overline{AB}$ at $Q$ and $\overline{DB}$ at $R.$ Given that $PQ = 735$ and $QR = 112,$ find $RC.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-7": { s: String.raw`Let $n$ be the number of ordered quadruples $(x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4)$ of positive odd integers that satisfy $x_1 + x_2 + x_3 + x_4 = 98.$ Find $\frac{n}{100}.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-8": { s: String.raw`Except for the first two terms, each term of the sequence $1000,$ $x,$ $1000 - x,$ $\ldots$ is obtained by subtracting the preceding term from the one before that. The last term of the sequence is the first negative term encountered. What positive integer $x$ produces a sequence of maximum length?`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-aime-9": { s: String.raw`Two mathematicians take a morning coffee break each day. They arrive at the cafeteria independently, at random times between $9$ a.m. and $10$ a.m., and stay for exactly $m$ minutes. The probability that either one arrives while the other is in the cafeteria is $40\%,$ and $m = a - b\sqrt{c},$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are positive integers, and $c$ is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find $a + b + c.$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/aime/1998" },
"1998-ajhsme-1": { s: String.raw`For $x = 7,$ which of the following is the smallest?

(A) $\dfrac{6}{x}$  (B) $\dfrac{6}{x+1}$  (C) $\dfrac{6}{x-1}$  (D) $\dfrac{x}{6}$  (E) $\dfrac{x+1}{6}$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1998" },
"1998-ajhsme-10": { s: String.raw`Each of the letters $W,$ $X,$ $Y,$ and $Z$ represents a different integer in the set $\{1,2,3,4\},$ but not necessarily in that order. They satisfy$$\dfrac{W}{X}-\dfrac{Y}{Z}=1$$What is the sum of $W$ and $Y?$

(A) $3$  (B) $4$  (C) $5$  (D) $6$  (E) $7$`, u: "https://live.poshenloh.com/past-contests/amc8/1998" },
